{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"1793697956112","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"cc4","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. **Keep personal Chrome windows open.** Do not kill Chrome processes or reuse your personal profile. Use only the authorized dedicated test profile.\n\n2. Check MCP’s configured debug URL and port. Commands below assume `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; replace `9222` if configuration differs. In PowerShell:\n   ```powershell\n   Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 9222 -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n   ```\n   If another process owns that port, identify it. Do not terminate it blindly; choose an unused port and update MCP configuration to match.\n\n3. Launch Chrome with a separate profile. Run in **PowerShell**, not Bash:\n   ```powershell\n   $chrome = @(\n       \"$env:ProgramFiles\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\chrome.exe\"\n       \"${env:ProgramFiles(x86)}\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\chrome.exe\"\n       \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\chrome.exe\"\n   ) | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1\n\n   if (-not $chrome) { throw \"Chrome executable not found\" }\n\n   $profile = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA \"TDQ-Chrome-MCP-Test\"\n   & $chrome \"--remote-debugging-address=127.0.0.1\" \"--remote-debugging-port=9222\" \"--user-data-dir=$profile\" \"--no-first-run\" \"--no-default-browser-check\" \"about:blank\"\n   ```\n   If that test profile is already running without debugging enabled, close **only its windows**, then rerun.\n\n4. Verify endpoint:\n   ```powershell\n   Invoke-RestMethod -Uri \"http://127.0.0.1:9222/json/version\" -TimeoutSec 5\n   ```\n   Expect JSON containing `Browser` and `webSocketDebuggerUrl`. A listening port alone does not prove Chrome debugging works.\n\n5. Reconnect Chrome MCP using the matching endpoint. Reload MCP connection or restart MCP server if needed. Verify with a read-only tab-list call; confirm it shows the test browser.\n\n6. If endpoint still fails, check Chrome launch errors, port conflicts, and `chrome://policy` for remote-debugging restrictions. Do not bypass enterprise policy. Stop browser-dependent work until connection succeeds.\n\n**Security:** Keep debugging bound to loopback. Do not add `--remote-allow-origins=*`, expose the port through a firewall, or sign into personal accounts in the test profile. Close the test browser when finished."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae16b9fd-787a-4627-b3d2-77314812c3a4","uuid":"923d468f-b7fb-4501-a647-79d8386133d6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T09:26:12.483Z"}
